WEBVTT

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.250
May 20th.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.820
The advent of a stalker who sends me cola.

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:12.090
Actually, I don't know yet if it was a stalker.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.360
I mean, why is he doing this anyway?

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.380
I still don't understand it, but...

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:20.240
Think... think, who could it be?

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:26.980
What's that?

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.190
Someone left these outside.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.460
The note says, "You can have them."

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:37.090
This is Komaki-san, a substitute manager who works harder than the actual manager.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.100
She makes Japanese sweets herself,

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.850
and we sell as many as we can in the shop.

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.850
Should we report this to the police?

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.600
No, not necessary.

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.700
Leave them in the fridge.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:50.980
We'll drink them later.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.140
We're drinking them?

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.300
They're for you, right?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.110
We don't know where they came from.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:01:01.620
Still, there was a suspect who came to mind.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.040
Someone has been launching plastic bottle rockets around here lately.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.410
Let's check out the launch site tomorrow after school.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.470
Why is he launching them on a weekday afternoon?

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.970
A part of me was curious.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.900
I usually bought lunch at the school cafeteria,

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:02.280
since if I asked my parents to make lunch,
they'd just pack up leftovers from the bar.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.910
The oyako-don here is great.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.910
It's a bit too sweet, though.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.420
You think so?

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.670
It seems the transfer student likes rich flavoring.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:16.380
What's going on today?

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.420
You're not having lunch with Ryuushi.

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.760
I thought I'd try the cafeteria food for once.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.220
And it's not like I eat lunch with Ryuushi-san every day.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:28.640
She's having lunch with her basketball team.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.690
You don't have to be overly considerate, transfer student.

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:35.520
I have no choice but to keep calling him "transfer student",

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.860
even though that title is no longer appropriate.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.200
To be honest, I only vaguely remember his real name.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.820
Didn't Ryuushi call him by his last name?

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.580
Let's see... was it "Miwa-kun"?

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:49.080
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.580
How about I take the transfer student there?

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.420
There's no telling who I'll be up against.

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:02.430
I need a reliable gentleman who can defend the helpless Maekawa-san...

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.840
Actually, never mind.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.930
Don't worry about it.

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:10.430
See ya, Miwa-kun.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.940
Yeah.

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.940
Maybe it wasn't "Miwa-kun".

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:23.490
Either way, it doesn't fit my character, so I've decided to keep calling him the transfer student.

00:04:28.490 --> 00:04:30.450
Why are you eating in front of the shop?

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.460
It's my front-row seat.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.380
I wonder why he's launching those.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.470
Maybe he's trying to reach space.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:44.720
Even though they're just propelled by water?

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:50.010
I think everything flying vertically is trying to reach space.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.140
Is that right?

00:04:52.140 --> 00:04:55.560
Escape from gravity, you know?

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.610
But it's only make-believe.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.240
I guess it's hard to actually achieve it.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.070
Thanks for the meal.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.370
It was delicious.

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.410
Glad you liked it.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.160
I'll start wearing a banana costume tomorrow.

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:14.330
Don't you dare!

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:17.540
See you tomorrow, then.

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.750
Bye!

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:25.050
"Plastic bottle rockets should be launched in an open area."

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.840
That's what my elementary school teacher taught me.

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:33.140
That abandoned forestry school nearby fits that description.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.750
Yo!

00:05:57.710 --> 00:05:59.080
You're...

00:05:59.080 --> 00:06:02.000
Are you the one who left that cola behind our shop?

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:04.420
Yeah, that was me.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:05.670
Why for me?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:09.840
I'm your.... fan.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.300
That sounds like a lie.

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:14.470
It's true! I'm not lying.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.100
You're not in a strange getup like usual.

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:22.860
How rude! It's authentic cosplay.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:25.360
Oh, forgive my rudeness.

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.990
Did you happen to see these flying around?

00:06:27.990 --> 00:06:29.860
Huh? Yeah.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.490
Why are you launching them?

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:35.370
Well, it's just a hobby.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:38.870
I can't launch a real rocket into space,

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:40.630
so I launch these instead.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.590
Space, huh?

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:44.250
Isn't outer space great?

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.380
The deep sea isn't too bad either with its many mysteries.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:50.220
He must be a native of this city.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:53.680
Are you, uh, good with your hands?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.970
Yeah, I'm all right.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:59.940
I always got As in shop in middle school.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:01.440
Excellent!

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:05.110
The thing is, I want you to make plastic bottle rockets for me.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:05.980
What?

00:07:05.980 --> 00:07:06.940
Have you made them before?

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:10.460
Yes, in elementary school craft classes.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:11.950
I knew it.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:15.240
They're still teaching those.

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:17.200
I'm not asking you to do it for free.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.410
How about this much for each?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:21.170
Five hundred yen?

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.120
Five thousand!

00:07:23.380 --> 00:07:25.290
I want you to make a lot of them.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:30.170
Just bring them to me when you finish.

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:31.880
I want to conduct test flights.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:38.350
The easiest way to balance a scale with <i>danger</i> on one side

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:41.890
is to place <i>reward</i> on the other.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:46.400
All right, I accept. Let me make rockets.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.490
It's my second night job!

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:54.030
Maekawa-san is always there to help!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:03.750
Um... I wonder what Maekawa-san will bring.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.500
I wonder. I don't have the slightest idea.

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:09.260
I guess not.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.160
Have a cup of tea.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.670
Here, tea.

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:54.180
Have some tea.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:01.680
Have a cup of tea.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:05.940
Here, tea.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.190
Have some tea.

00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:14.320
Have a cup of tea.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:14.820
Here, tea.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:15.450
Have some tea.

00:09:15.450 --> 00:09:16.110
Have a cup of tea.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:16.700
Here, tea.

00:09:16.700 --> 00:09:17.570
Have some tea.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:22.830
I'm home!

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:25.370
What's with the getup?

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:27.920
Since I will be the scientist of the day,

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.710
I went back to the basics of cosplay, the lab coat!

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:33.010
By the way, these glasses are fake.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:35.470
Whoa! Cool!

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:38.050
What's in the bag?

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:41.880
These are materials for plastic bottle rockets.

00:09:41.880 --> 00:09:46.810
Meme-san asked Touwa and the transfer student to help me make them.

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.020
You'll join us, right, Ryuushi?

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.650
Hmm... I don't know how, but...

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.400
And it's Ryuuko!

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.110
Don't make a habit of calling me that!

00:09:56.110 --> 00:09:58.320
No problem! I'll teach you how.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.620
Maybe I can give it a try!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.660
But what's gotten into Touwa-san's mom all of a sudden?

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:04.500
Who knows?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.500
Touwa, where's Meme-san's room?

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.500
She said there were things we needed for the mission.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.550
I'll show her the way.

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.430
Hey, Maekawa-san.

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:22.430
Call me "sensei" while we're working!

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.520
Maekawa-sensei...

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:26.180
Yes, what is it?

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:31.520
Is this related to the plastic bottle rocket we saw earlier, by any chance?

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:34.480
Keen observation!

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:39.410
But you don't have to be versed in floriography to appreciate flowers, transfer student.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:44.160
I was wondering what this has to do with Erio and me.

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.370
I also don't know anything about floriography.

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:50.920
Sorry.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.590
Okay.

00:10:55.590 --> 00:10:58.510
It's time for Maekawa-sensei's craft class!

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:04.760
Is it just me, or am I being used to separate these two?

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.000
Do you remember how to make one, Touwa?

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:08.600
I don't.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.310
I thought we all learned it in elementary school.

00:11:11.310 --> 00:11:16.980
Um... I brought it home and had my mom help me.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.700
All right, you're a trainee then.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.280
Everybody, take a plastic bottle.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.760
Next, take a jet nozzle.

00:11:25.040 --> 00:11:27.040
Attach it to the top.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.880
I did it, Maekawa-sensei!

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.880
Put it down for now, and take a second bottle.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:42.130
Leave some space at the bottom, and cut it off.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.850
We only have one knife, so we'll take turns.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.560
A craft class sure brings back memories!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:53.190
The key is to cut the bottle by rotating it forward, not by moving the knife.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:56.150
Just like peeling an apple.

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.900
Ryuushi-san and I proceeded without problems.

00:12:06.910 --> 00:12:11.410
Loosen up a little, but hold firmly.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.960
This isn't a scrap factory.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.920
But keep a firm grip.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:33.600
Good enough.

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:37.110
Next, let's trim them evenly with scissors.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:39.190
The key here is to cut from the bottom.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:41.940
Done!

00:12:43.080 --> 00:12:45.530
We're launching the rockets tomorrow.

00:12:45.530 --> 00:12:46.320
Tomorrow?

00:12:46.320 --> 00:12:52.000
We have orders from Meme-san
to meet at the nearest beach at 11 A.M.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:57.170
We have no time for test flights,
so not all of them will fly straight up.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:13:01.920
Unless you hang them with strings from space.

00:13:03.940 --> 00:13:05.930
I have high expectations of you, Touwa.

00:13:07.180 --> 00:13:12.560
I'm sure these rockets will fly, with your space-power!

00:13:13.430 --> 00:13:17.440
Next, it was time for the subsistence cooking class.

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:22.740
We all agreed to make things we like, myself included.

00:13:23.820 --> 00:13:28.030
I can taste the sweetness of adolescence just from the sight of them in aprons.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:29.990
This is the third one I made!

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:32.040
Oh? Meme-san made those?

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:34.910
But I made them—

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:35.750
Right, right!

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.040
Good girl!

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.550
After about 20 minutes, they said they were done.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:50.300
It was Erio's and my turn.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:56.730
I guess I'll just make something easy.

00:14:10.280 --> 00:14:14.620
Why did everyone make something that involves putting stuff on top of rice?

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:15.700
It's easy.

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:16.250
I'm good at it.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.370
It's ham.

00:14:17.370 --> 00:14:22.000
I would write "let's study Japanese harder" on the last girl's assignment.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.920
I made oyako-don.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:27.010
It might be a bit cold now.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:28.930
Yummy!

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:32.510
I'm glad you like it.

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:35.770
I made oyako-don without chicken.

00:14:35.770 --> 00:14:38.770
Then it's missing the "oya" part!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.810
Wouldn't it be called egg-don instead?

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:47.780
But there's a rumor that Niwa-kun likes oyako-don, so...

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.740
Maybe she heard it from Maekawa-san?

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:53.530
I recall raving about the cafeteria's oyako-don.

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:55.120
Anyway, enjoy!

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:56.790
Chow down!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:03.130
She must have deliberately made the same thing as Maekawa-san.

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:05.300
Very provocative.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.800
Thanks...

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:11.890
How's it taste?

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:13.100
Is there...

00:15:13.100 --> 00:15:14.640
pineapple in this?

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:18.770
Yup! Ryuuko-san loves pineapple in sweet and sour pork!

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:22.650
I like sweet ones, too.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.150
Hey, is it yummy? Huh?

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:29.650
My mother taught me not to talk while eating.

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.990
I ended up eating the whole thing.

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.990
I forced myself to.

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:38.700
The remaining two are not particularly interesting, so I'll introduce them at the same time.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:40.830
Fried-egg-don.

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:42.960
Ham-don.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:44.840
Thank you for the meal!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.760
You're not going home yet, Maekawa-san?

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.470
No.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:52.470
Then would you like to stay?

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:53.300
Huh?

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:56.430
Well, it's dark out.

00:15:56.430 --> 00:15:57.560
It's dangerous.

00:15:57.560 --> 00:15:59.310
There might be aliens.

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:02.060
I guess I'll take you up on the offer!

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:03.600
That's outrageous!

00:16:03.600 --> 00:16:05.520
What do you think, Niwa-kun?

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:09.480
As long as Meme-san and Erio are fine with it...

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:11.530
<i>Why</i> are you allowing this?

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:13.780
This isn't my house, so...

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:14.570
Right?

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.570
Right.

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.950
Then, then... maybe I'll stay too!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:21.580
Wh-What do you say?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.250
I guess it's fine?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.000
Then I'll go get my change of clothes.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:29.380
You can borrow mine.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:33.470
Okay, then.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.890
I guess I will.

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:37.260
You should.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:39.890
You should!

00:16:41.770 --> 00:16:45.020
It's like the sound I heard in the mountains where I grew up.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.400
The sound... of something flying in the sky.

00:16:48.980 --> 00:16:51.570
There was an Air Force base near our house,

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.990
but I wonder what's flying around here?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.410
Could it be...

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:56.740
UFOs?

00:16:59.030 --> 00:17:00.290
Hi!

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:01.790
Hi-ho!

00:17:01.790 --> 00:17:04.670
I took a quick shower!

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.130
It's so hot!

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:08.290
Where's Maekawa-san?

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.800
She's passed out by the porch.

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:12.050
What about Erio?

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:15.050
She's cooling Maekawa-san with a fan.

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:20.310
It was a ruckus until just now, because of the bathroom incident.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:28.560
Why is she taking a bath with her clothes on?

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:29.980
Oops.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.320
Hear that?

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:32.230
What?

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.900
Coordinate...

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.570
X-axis or Y-axis?

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:37.030
What about her?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:42.290
Why did she pass out after just a minute in hot water?

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.330
Good blood circulation?

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:45.500
Not... not enough blood!

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:48.080
That's the worst combination!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:50.500
Here.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:51.880
Thanks.

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:56.930
It sounds like something is flying in the sky.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.090
Yup.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:00.180
I wonder if a comet's falling?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.760
I hear they can predict that years in advance.

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:06.350
Don't be so serious all the time!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.860
Actually, tomorrow...

00:18:09.860 --> 00:18:11.860
is my birthday!

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:13.860
Oh, really?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:14.780
Yep.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.030
I see.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:19.820
It's a day early, but happy birthday.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.410
Cheers!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:29.540
I guess I want something special to happen on my birthday.

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:31.590
Like a comet crashing down with a bang!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:37.340
Let's celebrate together tomorrow, after we're done at the beach.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:42.970
Celebrating your birthday with others may not be anything special,

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:44.720
but I think it's important.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.810
I'd like that.

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:51.150
Yeah, that would be the best!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:55.610
I decided to stay on the spur of the moment,

00:18:55.610 --> 00:18:57.490
but it's a little embarrassing.

00:18:59.400 --> 00:19:02.410
Staying at a male classmate's house...

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:03.330
Is it?

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:04.200
It is!

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:05.790
I mean,

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:09.870
I always see Ryuushi-san sleeping in the middle of class.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.380
Don't be peeking!

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:13.340
And it's Ryuuko!

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:15.630
Sleeping in the same room aside—

00:19:16.380 --> 00:19:17.510
Ryuushi-san?

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:19.800
Same room?

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.640
I won't be in the same one as you, right?

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.180
N-No.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.180
Right! Yup!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:31.230
A-About what we talked about earlier...

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.770
E-Earlier?

00:19:34.440 --> 00:19:35.770
Are you ready to answer?

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:39.440
I am!

00:19:39.440 --> 00:19:42.740
If this happened at this very moment...

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:47.080
Hypothetically, Erio's old classmates are picking on her.

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:49.620
And I happen to witness it.

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:51.210
Yes.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.960
Then I would probably side with her.

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:58.130
Although that would be very foolish.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.260
But still...

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:02.970
I don't want to be so wise that I ignore her.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:05.760
If Ryuushi-san were there too,

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.600
you should just kick me from behind.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:13.150
I can't drag you into trouble.

00:20:13.150 --> 00:20:16.730
Even if I wind up isolated, I can still somehow manage.

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:21.570
Hypothetically, at this very moment...

00:20:22.400 --> 00:20:26.320
I couldn't side with Touwa-san if that happens.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:27.990
Right.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.740
But...

00:20:30.750 --> 00:20:31.790
But!

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:35.250
I think I would side with you!

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:43.760
Mako-chan!

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:45.640
What is it?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.100
You'll catch a cold if you stay out too long.

00:20:48.100 --> 00:20:50.020
So hurry up!

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.600
Got it!

00:20:55.850 --> 00:20:58.230
Four-pointer... I guess.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:07.660
Who would've thought I'd be going to the sea with the transfer student under such circumstances?

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:08.780
Beep beep!

00:21:09.370 --> 00:21:13.290
When we arrived with Erio on
our memorable beach the next day,

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:14.960
there was another visitor.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.750
It's the alien-stalker!

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:19.540
Who's that?

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:20.420
Hello.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.340
Did Touwa Meme ask you to come?

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:24.380
Y-Yes!

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.680
Then prepare for the launch, everyone.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.680
I'll help out if you need me.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:33.930
Okay!

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:40.020
My adolescent life is at stake.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:41.900
I'm counting on you!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.910
Honestly, I don't know how I ended up here.

00:21:47.860 --> 00:21:50.410
I don't even know what all this has to do with me.

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.540
I feel like I'm just going with the flow.

00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.750
But still, that's fine.

00:21:54.750 --> 00:21:58.920
It can't hurt to help others acquire
adolescence points once in a while.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:01.880
I'm the Adolescence Boy, after all.

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:04.550
I live my life so honestly that it's foolish.

00:23:40.850 --> 00:23:44.270
Erio, Ryuushi-san, and I can't get a conversation going: -1

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.360
Eating girls' hand-cooked food: +3

00:23:46.360 --> 00:23:49.610
A night with Ryuushi-san and Maekawa-san under one roof: +3

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:52.780
Seeing Ryuushi-san and Maekawa-san in just bath towels: +5!

00:23:52.780 --> 00:23:55.580
No, 100! 10,000! Uh... oh...

00:23:55.580 --> 00:23:58.500
Talking to Ryuushi-san under the night sky: +4

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.790
Helping others with their adolescence: +3

00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:03.210
Current adolescence points total: -1

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:05.630
Next time: Tsiolkovsky's Prayer.

00:24:05.630 --> 00:24:09.050
Hey, Granny, is God an alien?
